    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Gunnar Henderson** (74.56) anchoring the offense as our clear top-tier starts. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Michael McGreevy, where a favorable park factor and a solid pitching matchup projection (4.51 xERA) allow his base production to swell, while **Gunnar Henderson** exploits a massive park factor boost at home against Jacob Lopez. Though **Gunnar Henderson** faces a slight negative platoon penalty, the aggressive, hitter-friendly environment elevates his ceiling significantly. **Coby Mayo** (65.10) also emerges as a high-value play despite hitting lower in the order, as his exposure to that same favorable environment against Lopez provides a substantial boost to his base output.\n\nRegarding our bench decisions, **Miguel Vargas** (51.20) was the primary outlier left on the sidelines. He fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace players like **Josh Lowe** (50.17) or **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (49.18). The optimizer ultimately sided with **Josh Lowe** due to his dynamic platoon advantage against right-handed pitching and a rare opportunity to exploit a slow-delivery pitcher to hunt stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Kyle Tucker** (52.14); while he remains a must-start, he faces a daunting matchup against Chris Sale (2.94 xERA), which suppresses his overall efficiency score significantly below his typical elite baseline. \n\nToday\u2019s slate is heavily impacted by the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, introducing volatility if these projected batting orders shift. **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci** are currently carrying heavy weight due to projected leadoff spots, but should their positions move down in the order, their efficiency scores will likely recalibrate downward. We are prioritizing high-contact, high-speed profiles in these matchups, keeping a close eye on wind conditions that could provide extra lift for **Heliot Ramos** and **Marcell Ozuna**, both of whom benefit from favorable park winds to bolster their raw power numbers.",
